WEBVTT

00:10:30.009 --> 00:10:31.160
Uh, oh!

00:10:31.184 --> 00:10:32.398
Audience: (Laughter)

00:10:32.422 --> 00:10:34.947
(Video) Diver 1: I think we have
their attention ...

00:10:34.971 --> 00:10:37.501
Richard Pyle: When you start
talking like Donald Duck,

00:10:37.525 --> 00:10:40.098
there's no situation in the world
that can seem tense.

00:10:40.122 --> 00:10:42.056
(Laughter)

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:44.994
So we're down there --
this is at 400 feet.

00:10:45.018 --> 00:10:48.892
That's looking straight up, by the way,
to give a sense of how far the surface is.

00:10:48.916 --> 00:10:51.164
And if you're a biologist
and know about sharks,

00:10:51.188 --> 00:10:54.438
and you want to assess,
how much jeopardy am I really in here,

00:10:54.462 --> 00:10:58.564
there's one question that sort of jumps
to the forefront of your mind immediately,